d ultrasonography can no longer be ignored</article-title><source>Scand J Rheumatol</source><year>2003</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/03009740310000058</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ostergaard M, Szkudlarek M. Imaging in rheumatoid arthritis&#x02014;why MRI and ultrasonography can no longer be ignored. Scand J Rheumatol. 2003;32:63&#x02013;73. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12737323</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haavardsholm</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000f8;yesen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>&#x000d8;stergaard</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schildvold</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kvien</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Magnetic resonance imaging findings in 84 patients with early rheumatoid arthritis: bone marrow edema predicts erosive progression</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>2008</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>794</fpage><lpage>800</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/ard.2007.071977</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Haavardsholm EA, B&#x000f8;yesen P, &#x000d8;stergaard M, Schildvold A, Kvien TK. Magnetic resonance imaging findings in 84 patients with early rheumatoid arthritis: bone marrow edema predicts erosive progression. Ann Rheum Dis. 2008;67:794&#x02013;800. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17981915</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taouli</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaim</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterfy</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Lynch</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stork</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Guermazi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Rheumatoid arthritis of the hand and wrist: comparison of three imaging techniques</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>2004</year><volume>182</volume><fpage>937</fpage><lpage>943</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Taouli B, Zaim S, Peterfy CG, Lynch JA, Stork A, Guermazi A, et al. Rheumatoid arthritis of the hand and wrist: comparison of three imaging techniques. AJR Am J Roentgenol 2004;182:937&#x02013;43. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15039167</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Savnik</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Malmskov</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomsen</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bretlau</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Graff</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Nielsen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>MRI of the arthritic small joints: comparison of extremity MRI (0.2&#x000a0;T) vs high-field MRI (1.5&#x000a0;T)</article-title><source>Eur Radiol</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>1030</fpage><lpage>1038</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s003300000709</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Savnik A, Malmskov H, Thomsen HS, Bretlau T, Graff LB, Nielsen H, et al. MRI of the arthritic small joints: comparison of extremity MRI (0.2&#x000a0;T) vs high-field MRI (1.5&#x000a0;T). Eur Radiol. 2001;11:1030&#x02013;8. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11419149</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pers